{"name":"Grenade","hex":"#c32149","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grenade","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small explosive device, designed to be thrown by hand or launched using a rifle, grenade launcher, or rocket.","A pomegranate."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To use grenade(s) upon.","Of an engine: to be violently wrecked so that the internal components burst out."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grenade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grenade","blocks":[{"text":"A grenade is a small explosive projectile. It can be thrown by hand, launched by a rifle attachment, or launched by a dedicated launcher. A modern hand grenade generally consists of an explosive charge (\"filler\"), a detonator mechanism, an internal striker to trigger the detonator, and an arming safety secured by a transport safety. The user removes the transport safety pins before throwing, and once the grenade leaves the hand the arming safety gets released, allowing the striker to trigger a primer that ignites a fuze, which burns down to the detonator and explodes the main charge."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Victory_Show_Cosby_UK_06-09-2015_WW2_re-enactment_Trade_stalls_Militaria_personal_gear_replicas_reprod.originals_zaphad1_Flickr_CCBY2.0_Hand_grenades_etc_IMG_3865.jpg/330px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grenade","wikidata":"Q173517"},{"title":"Grenade (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Grenade\" is a song by American singer and songwriter Bruno Mars from his debut studio album, Doo-Wops & Hooligans (2010). The pop and power pop song was written and produced by the Smeezingtons with additional songwriting by Brody Brown, Claude Kelly, and Andrew Wyatt. The song was developed from an unreleased track with similar lyrical themes. \"Grenade\" was completely rearranged and re‑recorded two days before the album \"was supposed to be handed in\". The lyrics carry a message of unrequited love and how Mars's heart was broken, despite his best efforts to show her his love. Elektra Records released the song as the second promotional single and as the second official single, to contemporary hit and rhythmic contemporary stations in the United States in October 2010."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/36/BrunoMarsGrenade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grenade_(song)","wikidata":"Q166791"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Liquid_fire_granades_Chania.jpg/500px-Liquid_fire_granades_Chania.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Liquid_fire_granades_Chania.jpg/1280px-Liquid_fire_granades_Chania.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Liquid_fire_granades_Chania.jpg/500px-Liquid_fire_granades_Chania.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hand grenades filled with Greek fire; surrounded by caltrops (10th–12th centuries National Historical Museum, Athens, Greece)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALiquid_fire_granades_Chania.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/M%C5%8Dko_Sh%C5%ABrai_Ekotoba.jpg/500px-M%C5%8Dko_Sh%C5%ABrai_Ekotoba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/M%C5%8Dko_Sh%C5%ABrai_Ekotoba.jpg/1280px-M%C5%8Dko_Sh%C5%ABrai_Ekotoba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/M%C5%8Dko_Sh%C5%ABrai_Ekotoba.jpg/500px-M%C5%8Dko_Sh%C5%ABrai_Ekotoba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedi